The campaign begins with JISOO &#8212; who in 2024 became the first musician to be the face of the London fashion house &#8212; in &#8220;The Enigma,&#8221; the first of the four videos. Shot in the style of an audition tape by Oliver Hadlee Pearch, it shows the performer modeling Self-Portrait&#8217;s faux leather skirt and checkered knit blazer, appearing bubbly and confident in herself in front of the camera.

&#8220;Maybe we&#8217;re not supposed to have everything figured out,&#8221; JISOO muses in the clip. &#8220;I always liked wandering.&#8221;

For the partnership, JISOO worked closely with the brand&#8217;s founder and creative director, Han Chong. In a statement, the K-pop star said, &#8220;I was so excited to star in this new series of short films &#8230; it allowed me to try something completely new, and each character I played required something different from me.&#8221;

&#8220;The evolution of the character&#8217;s wardrobe was how I found the nuance in each performance, and it was a real collaboration with Han and I on finding the subtlety in each role I was going to be playing,&#8221; she continued. &#8220;I have worn Self-Portrait for many years, and the pieces make me feel like I can do anything &#8212; this time, they let me dream that I could be anyone.&#8221;

Chong also praised the global star in a statement. &#8220;Having worked with JISOO for a few years now, she really has become a big part of our brand&#8217;s story and fabric. For this latest project together, we wanted to do something that meets JISOO where she is today; an incredible artist with range and a chameleonic edge as a performer,&#8221; he said. &#8220;We always talk about the Self-Portrait woman as being multifaceted, and JISOO really brings that to life through her performance in these short films.&#8221;

JISOO&#8217;s latest fashion campaign comes as she&#8217;s embarking on a new solo era musically. On Friday (Sept. 4), she released single &#8220;Click.&#8221;

